<title>EGYPT: Yield rises on Egyptian six-month T-bil.</title>
<headline>Yield rises on Egyptian six-month T-bil.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on Egyptian 182-day treasury bills rose to 10.259 percent from 10.258 percent at the previous auction on September 9.</p>
<p>The Central Bank of Egypt announced the following details (values in pounds, previous week in brackets):</p>
<p>Maturity date: Mar 18, 1997 (Mar 11, 1997)</p>
<p>Average yield: 10.259 percent (10.258)</p>
<p>Value of bids accepted: 849.875 milion (739.550 million)</p>
<p>Value of bids: 849.975 million (851.550 million)</p>
<p>Range accepted: 9.999-10.287 percent (9.999-10.284)</p>
<p>Range of bids: 9.999-10.600 percent (9.999-10.600)</p>
<p>Number of bids accepted: 107 (115)</p>
<p>Number of bids: 110 (122)</p>
<p>$1 = 3.40 pounds</p>
<p>-- Cairo reporting unit +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
